# BoardTrack Access Control Plan

## 1. Purpose

The purpose of this access control plan is to implement role-based access control (RBAC) in the BoardTrack system using PostgreSQL. It aims to protect business records and ensure that users can only perform actions allowed by their assigned roles.

## 2. User Roles and Permissions

| Role | Permissions |
|---|---|
| Administrator | Full access to create, read, update, and delete business records. |
| Staff | Can create, read, and update records but cannot delete records. |
| Tenant | Can only view their own lease, payments, and utility bills. |
| Application Runtime | Uses a controlled database account to perform application operations. |

## 3. Database Roles

| PostgreSQL Role | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| boardtrack_owner | LOGIN | Owns database objects and performs migrations. |
| boardtrack_admin_grp | NOLOGIN | Provides administrator-level database privileges. |
| app_runtime_grp | NOLOGIN | Provides database privileges required by the application. |
| app_readonly_grp | NOLOGIN | Provides read-only database access. |
| boardtrack_app | LOGIN | Runtime account used by the Node.js application. |

## 4. Security Measures

- Apply the principle of least privilege.
- Prevent staff from deleting business records.
- Restrict tenant access to their own records through application filtering and database views where appropriate.
- Do not use the database owner account for normal application operations.
- Keep database passwords outside the source code repository.
- Avoid granting unnecessary SUPERUSER or CREATEROLE privileges.

## 5. Verification

Database permissions will be checked using PostgreSQL privilege queries and test operations. The verification will confirm that the assigned roles receive only their intended permissions.

## 6. Expected Result

The implementation should provide an additional database security layer that supports the existing application permissions of BoardTrack.